{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788589161318335307,"compiled_state":{"alias":"foliated-correct-arcticfox","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"69248e99354f35505fcd8945b4ddc09880d3c823c32bacd4f2a415cdb434f1fe","event_uuid":"0ee255b5-7779-4b78-9387-a939f0a7b19f","position":{"commit_sha":"6a3ca2c52e5e9f1fb880d8d2170be6aafb44091a","position":"1788584510722419001-0ee255b5-7779-4b78-9387-a939f0a7b19f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"bcdd5c4fa2e7ebbf34c411b8cdbbdd449648b27bfb8527bbe2aba7fd95e04652","event_uuid":"c55f81bd-84a4-4ef4-a6d4-88887ee846f9","position":{"commit_sha":"0b1d1924c50cb99dec7c7665119d32033bf0d7d9","position":"1788584547529214001-c55f81bd-84a4-4ef4-a6d4-88887ee846f9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"4d369c4baf0e58f38a493c7099d9dc3c390cccb6ddf48678cd54b7a38a3e1466","event_uuid":"39f4e277-7272-4601-ba3d-be2f870d4b9d","position":{"commit_sha":"61a5ed343a5c7159aea355cc85c3826a98e66a30","position":"1788584580986430001-39f4e277-7272-4601-ba3d-be2f870d4b9d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788584510722419001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"39f4e277-7272-4601-ba3d-be2f870d4b9d","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"3e32-a859-2153-4a1b"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nOn `origin/main` at `25d1d683e55a`, `make worktree name=comment-remediation-3e32` selected `/opt/homebrew/bin/uv` 0.12.9 while `pyproject.toml` requires 0.12.7. `uv venv` correctly refused the mismatch, but the Makefile catch-all handler reported that Python 3.12 was unavailable and advised `uv python install 3.12`. Running the same target with the existing 0.12.7 binary created a Python 3.12.13 venv, proving that diagnosis false.\n\nThe exact uv pin and its refusal are intentional. This bug is the misleading classification of every `uv venv` failure as a missing interpreter. It is distinct from `princely-courageous-milksnake`, which repairs the machine-local updater uv selection.\n\n## Approach\nKeep fail-fast provisioning. Add a preflight that compares the selected uv executable/version with the repository exact required version before `uv venv`, and emit a mismatch-specific diagnostic naming the executable, actual version, and required version. Preserve the existing interpreter-unavailable diagnostic for a compatible uv whose venv operation fails.\n\nExtend the real-Makefile subprocess tests with controlled uv stubs for both failure classes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A selected uv version that violates `[tool.uv].required-version` fails before provisioning and names the selected path, actual version, and required version.\n- [ ] The mismatch path does not claim Python is unavailable or advise installing the already-available pinned interpreter.\n- [ ] A compatible uv whose `uv venv --python <pin>` fails still reports the pinned-interpreter provisioning failure.\n- [ ] `make worktree` continues to propagate either provisioning failure without printing its success message.\n- [ ] Focused Makefile worktree/python-pin tests, lint, and typecheck pass.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"Makefile","reason":"Classify selected uv version mismatch separately from interpreter provisioning failure."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_worktree_python_pin.py","reason":"Drive the real Makefile with uv stubs covering incompatible-version and interpreter-unavailable diagnostics."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["devex","makefile","diagnostics","uv"],"ticket_id":"1f58-ba19-afac-445e","ticket_type":"bug","title":"make worktree misreports a uv version mismatch as a missing Python interpreter","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["0ee255b5-7779-4b78-9387-a939f0a7b19f","c55f81bd-84a4-4ef4-a6d4-88887ee846f9","39f4e277-7272-4601-ba3d-be2f870d4b9d"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788589161318335307,"uuid":"7b60c6ce-f70e-4a1b-b81f-8b2ac7c35a54"}